    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for the **Austin Waves** is anchored by a high-upside core, with **Jackson Merrill** (73.24) serving as our strongest play. His matchup against Roki Sasaki is highlighted by a generous 14% boost from the opposing SP\u2019s skill set and a perfect 100% stolen base opportunity rating, which is critical given our heavy emphasis on speed. Similarly, **Nasim Nunez** (70.43) offers exceptional value; despite a lower base projection, his presence in the lineup against Trevor Rogers is amplified by the pitcher's slow delivery, which provides a tangible path to a stolen base that the optimizer aggressively rewards. **Kyle Tucker** (69.85) remains a cornerstone, maintaining a high floor against Walker Buehler, while **Andy Pages** (65.74) and **Josh Jung** (64.84) benefit from favorable park factors and SP vulnerabilities, respectively.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card involved keeping **Curtis Mead** (58.36) on the bench. He fell just short of the cut despite a 16% park boost against Trevor Rogers, ultimately losing out to the defensive versatility and platoon optimization of our starting MI/UTIL mix. We also evaluated **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (57.70), but the stiff challenge posed by Nathan Eovaldi\u2019s 3.36 xERA created too high of a barrier for him to crack the starting nine. Managers should monitor the 45% rain risk for the games featuring **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Nasim Nunez**; these contests remain highly volatile. With several lineups currently pending, we are proceeding with our best-estimated projections for **Drake Baldwin**, **Nolan Schanuel**, and **Cole Carrigg**, but will be ready to pivot if official confirmation shifts our tactical advantage.",
